The discussion about the near impossibility of the
"never identify anything" conduct made me realize
how many "conduct breaking" actions I didn't even
know existed for that proposed conduct, which led to
this related proposal:

As each conduct is broken, it would be nice if the
game messaged the player "so much for conduct %s
[you clumsy oaf(*)]"; that way at least you'd see the
conduct evaporating at the point where you broke it,
and so have some clue _how_ you broke it, not be
unpleasantly surprised later when checking via a
#conduct.

I'm often down to the usual last four conducts
before I make it off the first dungeon level, and it
isn't from _trying_ to break all the conducts, more
from not noticing them as they get broken, if that
makes sense.

This doesn't seem particularly hard to implement, or
a particularly burdensome distraction to the player
who isn't targeting any conducts; it might even be
controllable via a configuration file flag for folks
who don't want the messages. What would be the
downsides?

xanthian.

(*) Optional, a product of my personality traits.



